#: {{ux|de|Du hast einen Fehler '''gemacht'''.|inline=1|You '''made''' a mistake.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|of food, drinks, etc.}} to make, [[prepare]]
#: {{ux|de|'''Machst''' du heute das Essen?|inline=1|'''Are''' you '''making''' dinner today?}}
#: {{ux|de|sich eine Pizza '''machen'''|inline=1|to '''prepare''' a pizza for oneself}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|informal}} to [[do]], [[perform]], [[carry out]] {{gloss|to execute; to put into operation (an action)}}
#: {{ux|de|'''Mach''' es!|inline=1|'''Do''' it!}}
#: {{ux|de|Das '''hat''' er ganz allein '''gemacht'''!|inline=1|He '''has done''' that all by himself!}}
#: {{ux|de|ein Experiment '''machen'''|to '''perform''' an experiment|inline=1}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|with a noun}} to [[do]]; {{n-g|indicates an activity associated with a noun}}
#: {{ux|de|Sport '''machen'''|'''do''' sports|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|de|eine Party '''machen'''|'''have''' a party|inline=1}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[go]] {{gloss|to make the (specified) sound}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[make]] {{gloss|to cause or compel (to do something)}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|of difficulties, pain, etc.}} to [[cause]] {{gloss|to set off an event or action or produce as a result}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|with an adjective}} to [[make]] {{gloss|to cause to be}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|with a noun}} to [[make]] ({{m|de|aus}} (“into”)) {{gloss|to cause to become}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|usually not translated literally}} to [[make]] {{gloss|to have as a feature}} <!--Collins gives the example: "die Straße macht einen Knick" with the example "the road bends"-->
# {{lb|de|transitive|informal|colloquial}} to [[come to]], [[total]], [[cost]] {{gloss|to require the payment of}}
#: {{ux|de|Wie viel '''macht''' das?|inline=1|How much '''does''' that '''come to'''?}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|arithmetic}} to [[make]], [[be]] {{gloss|to have a sum of}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|informal|colloquial}} to [[make]] {{gloss|to earn, gain wages, profit, etc.}}
#: {{ux|de|Der Herr Müller ist echt reich; der '''macht''' mehr als 5000 im Monat.|Mr Müller is quite rich; he '''makes''' more than 5000 bucks per month.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[be]], [[play]] {{gloss|to act as the indicated role, especially in a performance}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|impersonal|colloquial}} to [[matter]] {{gloss|to be important}}
#: {{ux|de|Das '''macht''' nichts!|inline=1|That doesn't '''matter'''!}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive|with ''[[auf]]''}} to [[make]], make oneself out to be, [[act]], [[play]] {{gloss|to behave so as to give an appearance of being; to act as if one were (something, or a certain way)}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive|informal|euphemistic}} to [[do one's business]], do [[number two]] or [[number one]], [[go]] {{gloss|to defecate or urinate}}
