#: {{ux|de|{{q|childish}} klein '''machen'''|'''to go''' pee|inline=1}}
# {{lb|de|reflexive}} to [[do]] {{gloss|to fare or perform (well or poorly)}}
# {{lb|de|reflexive}} to [[look]] {{gloss|to have an appearance of being}}
#: {{ux|de|Der Mantel '''macht sich''' sehr schön.|The coat '''looks''' very nice.|inline=1}}
# {{lb|de|reflexive|_|dative|colloquial}} to [[get cracking]] ({{m|de|an}} (“on,” “with”)), [[get a move on]] (it), to [[get down]] ({{m|de|an}} (“to”)) (something); {{q|in imperative:}} [[come on]], [[let's go]] 


====Usage notes====
*Unlike English, the verb {{m|de|machen|t=[[make]]}} is used as a synonym for {{m|de|tun|t=[[do]]}} in most cases. However, ''tun'' cannot be used for the proper senses of ''machen''.
*The verb ''Machen'' can be combined with a number of different to create various expressions. These can often be translated into English with [[make]] or [[take]]. For many of these expressions, a more specific verb is available and is usually preferred in formal or written language.
*: {{uxi|de|Angaben machen|to provide information}}
*: {{uxi|de|eine Aufzeichnung machen|to keep a record}}
*: {{uxi|de|Ausflüchte machen|to make excuses}}
*: {{uxi|de|Bankrott/Pleite machen|to go bankrupt}}
*: {{uxi|de|eine Besorgung machen|to run an errand}}
*: {{uxi|de|ein Bett machen|to make a bed}}
*: {{uxi|de|Feierabend machen|to call it a day}}
*: {{uxi|de|Ferien machen|to take a vacation, to go on holiday}}
*: {{uxi|de|ein Feuer machen|to light a fire}}
*: {{uxi|de|ein Foto machen|to take a picture}}
*: {{uxi|de|Fortschritte machen|to make headway}}
*: {{uxi|de|Gewinn machen|to turn a profit}}
*: {{uxi|de|Kasse machen|to cash in}}
*: {{uxi|de|einen Krach machen|to make a racket}}
*: {{uxi|de|Notizen machen|to take notes}}
*: {{uxi|de|Platz machen|to make room}}
*: {{uxi|de|eine Reise machen|to take a trip}}
*: {{uxi|de|Schluss machen|to call it quits}}
*: {{uxi|de|Überstunden machen|to do overtime}}
*: {{uxi|de|Witze machen|to joke}}

